    </ParamChoice>
    <ParamBool id="swap_enable" name="Swapping Enable" group="General" default="false" visible="`${(&quot;mxs40tcpwm&quot; eq getIpBlockName()) || (&quot;mxs40ppss&quot; eq getIpBlockName())}`" editable="`${(&quot;mxs40tcpwm&quot; eq getIpBlockName()) || (&quot;mxs40ppss&quot; eq getIpBlockName())}`" desc="Selects how the buffered registers are applied on a TC (Terminal Count) event when a switch is pending. The Dead Time (DT) registers behave inversely to the others.&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Checked (switch):&lt;/b&gt; the active and buffered Compare 0, Compare 1 and Period values are swapped (exchanged) with each other on each switch. Dead time switching is not supported, so the buffered DT registers have no effect in this mode.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Unchecked (shadow copy):&lt;/b&gt; the buffered value is copied into the active register (Compare 0 Buff to Compare 0, Compare 1 Buff to Compare 1, Period Buff to Period, and buffered DT to DT); the buffered value itself is retained.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;" />

