    <!-- ====================== Timings row (line_out / line_compl_out interval measurement) ======================
         A dimension-style row drawn under line_compl_out (only when global Swapping Enable is OFF). It marks the
         duration, in counter counts, of each constant-level segment (T0, T1, ... Tx) of the line_out waveform
         across ONE full reference period. T0 starts at the period boundary and ends at the first line_out edge;
         each subsequent Ti runs between consecutive edges; the last interval ends at the period boundary.

         Reference period: period 1 when it is a full period (counter starts on the boundary), otherwise period 2
         (always a full 240 px period while swapping is off). The six raw line_out levels of that period
         (L0,L1,L2,apex,L3,L4) and their six segment-start X positions (X0,Xa,Xb,Xr,Xc,Xd, plus end XE) drive the
         edge detection: an edge exists between two adjacent segments iff their levels differ. Adjacent equal-level
         segments are merged so each Ti is one constant-level run.

         Duration: pixel width x counts-per-pixel. A full period is 240 px = cuw_period counts (single direction)
         or 2*cuw_period counts (up/down, the 240 px spans the up AND down legs), so the per-pixel scale recovers
         exact integer count differences from the (linear) segment X positions. -->
