    <!-- Clipped-tail flag: hide the trailing (window-edge) run's T# UNLESS the line_out graph actually draws a
         switching edge at x=800. The trailing run is the only run whose end reaches the edge (x&gt;=800; the
         running-max cap in cuw_tgShowDraw pins the last drawn run's end to exactly 800). Normally that run has no
         visible terminating edge (nothing is drawn past 800) so its duration is unmeasurable and it gets no T#.
         But when the periods tile the window exactly (last boundary cuw_b3_O &gt;= 800), the period-end boundary
         action flips the logical level (cuw_p3end differs from cuw_p3L4), AND the reaction is on-screen (dead-time
         does not push the activation edge past 800), the line_out now steps at x=800 (see cuw_co_4_0) - a real
         terminating edge - so the trailing period IS fully fit and measurable and MUST get a T#. One Shot always
         hides (Timings show only the first period). Hide (true) = oneShot, OR boundary not at 800, OR reaction
         pushed past 800, OR the level does not flip; otherwise show (false). -->
    <ParamBool id="cuw_tgLastClip" name="cuw_tgLastClip" group="General" default="`${cuw_oneShot || (cuw_b3_O &lt; 800) || ((cuw_b3 + ((cuw_p3end &gt; cuw_p3L4) ? cuw_dtOutPxE : 0)) &gt; 800) || ((cuw_p3end &lt;= cuw_p3L4) &amp;&amp; (cuw_p3L4 &lt;= cuw_p3end))}`" visible="false" editable="false" desc="" />
    <!-- Draw flag: a run-start with positive pixel width (skips zero-width / off-screen runs). Any run whose end
         reaches the window edge (x&gt;=800) shows no visible terminating edge there (the graph draws nothing past
         800, and an exactly-tiling boundary at 800 belongs to the next off-screen period), so its duration cannot
         be strictly measured and it must NOT get a T# - it is dropped here (which also removes it from the numeric
         T# group, since cuw_tgIdx / cuw_tgRunTot derive from this flag). Only the last drawn run ever reaches
         x&gt;=800 (the running-max cap pins its end to exactly 800), so this drops exactly the trailing, un-measurable
         run - including the exact-fill 3-period case. The test is &gt;= 800 (inclusive): in dead-time mode the
         trailing run's end is pre-clamped to exactly 800, so a strict &gt; 800 would miss it. cuw_tgLastClip is
         now conditional: true when the trailing run has no edge at x=800 (hidden), false when the line_out steps
         at x=800 (shown as a fully-fit period). -->
    <ParamString id="cuw_tgShowDraw0" name="cuw_tgShowDraw0" group="General" default="`${(cuw_tgShow0 eq 1) ? ((cuw_tgLX0 &lt; cuw_tgRunEnd0) ? ((cuw_tgLastClip &amp;&amp; (cuw_tgRunEnd0 &gt;= 800)) ? 0 : 1) : 0) : 0}`" visible="false" editable="false" desc="" />
