    <!-- Clipped-tail flag: hide the trailing (window-edge) run's T# UNLESS the line_compl_out graph actually draws
         a switching edge at x=800 (mirrors cuw_tgLastClip for the line_compl_out row). The trailing run is the
         only run whose end reaches the edge (x&gt;=800; the running-max cap in cuw_tcShowDraw pins the last drawn
         run's end to exactly 800). Normally that run has no visible terminating edge (nothing is drawn past 800)
         so its duration is unmeasurable and it gets no T#. But when the periods tile the window exactly (last
         boundary cuw_b3_C &gt;= 800), the period-end boundary action flips the logical level (cuw_p3end differs from
         cuw_p3L4), AND the compl reaction is on-screen (dead-time does not push the compl activation edge past
         800), the line_compl_out now steps at x=800 (see cuw_cn_4_0) - a real terminating edge - so the trailing
         period IS fully fit and measurable and MUST get a T#. One Shot always hides. Hide (true) = oneShot, OR
         boundary not at 800, OR reaction pushed past 800, OR the level does not flip; otherwise show (false). -->
    <ParamBool id="cuw_tcLastClip" name="cuw_tcLastClip" group="General" default="`${cuw_oneShot || (cuw_b3_C &lt; 800) || ((cuw_b3 + ((cuw_p3L4 &gt; cuw_p3end) ? cuw_dtComplPxE : 0)) &gt; 800) || ((cuw_p3end &lt;= cuw_p3L4) &amp;&amp; (cuw_p3L4 &lt;= cuw_p3end))}`" visible="false" editable="false" desc="" />
    <!-- Draw flag: a run-start with positive pixel width (skips zero-width / off-screen runs). Any run whose end
         reaches the window edge (x&gt;=800) shows no visible terminating edge there (the graph draws nothing past
         800, and an exactly-tiling boundary at 800 belongs to the next off-screen period; in dead-time mode the
         compl edge is delayed onto/past 800), so its duration cannot be strictly measured and it must NOT get a T#
         - it is dropped here (which also removes it from the numeric T# group, since cuw_tcIdx / cuw_tcRunTot
         derive from this flag). Only the last drawn run ever reaches x&gt;=800 (the running-max cap pins its end to
         exactly 800), so this drops exactly the trailing, un-measurable run - including the exact-fill 3-period
         case. The test is &gt;= 800 (inclusive): in dead-time mode the trailing run's end is pre-clamped to exactly
         800, so a strict &gt; 800 would miss it. cuw_tcLastClip is now conditional: true when the trailing run has
         no edge at x=800 (hidden), false when the line_compl_out steps at x=800 (shown as a fully-fit period). -->
    <ParamString id="cuw_tcShowDraw0" name="cuw_tcShowDraw0" group="General" default="`${(cuw_tcShow0 eq 1) ? ((cuw_tcLX0 &lt; cuw_tcRunEnd0) ? ((cuw_tcLastClip &amp;&amp; (cuw_tcRunEnd0 &gt;= 800)) ? 0 : 1) : 0) : 0}`" visible="false" editable="false" desc="" />
