    <!-- ============== Clipped-tail level freeze for line_out / line_compl_out (slots 4..8) ==============
         The line_out / line_compl_out polylines emit a fixed chain of vertices for every dynamic slot 4..8.
         Each waveform-transition X is analytically clamped to the 800 window edge, but the per-segment
         Y LEVELS are still computed from the full-period compare crossings. When the last visible slot is
         clipped (and the hidden slots collapse to x=800) all those clamped vertices stack at x=800 with
         ALTERNATING high/low levels, drawing a spurious vertical notch / peak at the end of the graph.
         To suppress it, each segment level is made "sticky": once a transition X reaches the window edge
         (&gt;= 800) the level is frozen to the previous in-window level, so the waveform runs flat to x=800 and
         stops. In-window transitions are unchanged, so periods that fully fit render exactly as before.
         cuw_co_* = line_out levels (350/380); cuw_cn_* = line_compl_out levels (430/400). Entry level holds
         the period-3 end level when slot 4 itself is degenerate (cuw_b3 &gt;= 800). The entry test uses the
         dead-time-shifted boundary (cuw_b3_O / cuw_b3_C) instead of the bare cuw_b3: this is identical when
         dead time is off (the shifted boundary equals cuw_b3), but in dead-time mode it also freezes the level
         when the activating period-3 end edge is delayed past the window edge (its shifted X is clamped to
         800). That keeps the output in its (delayed) inactive state to x=800 instead of drawing a spurious
         activation rise right at the window edge.
         END-OF-GRAPH TERMINAL-COUNT REACTION: when the last period fits EXACTLY to the window edge
         (cuw_b3 == 800) its terminal-count event dot is drawn at x=800 and the boundary action (SET / CLEAR /
         INVERT) is a real, on-screen event that must show as a step on the line outputs. The plain
         "cuw_b3_O &gt;= 800" freeze would hide it (cuw_b3_O is clamped to &lt;= 800, so it also fires on an exact
         fit). cuw_b3O_raw / cuw_b3C_raw are the UNCLAMPED activation-edge X (boundary + activating dead time):
         the level is frozen ONLY when that raw edge is &gt; 800, i.e. the reaction genuinely happens off-screen
         (period overflow, or a dead-time-delayed activation past the edge). When the raw edge is &lt;= 800 the
         reaction is on-screen and the boundary-action level (cuw_p4y0 / cuw_p4ny0) is drawn, so the exact-fit
         terminal count produces a visible end step. Non-fitting / dead-time-past-edge cases are unchanged. -->
    <ParamString id="cuw_b3O_raw" name="cuw_b3O_raw" group="General" default="`${cuw_b3 + ((cuw_p3end &gt; cuw_p3L4) ? cuw_dtOutPxE : 0)}`" visible="false" editable="false" desc="" />
